  "moon_jelly": {
    "title": "THIS ANIMAL HAS NO BRAIN OR HEART",
    "script": "A moon jelly can swim without a brain, a heart, or blood. Its body is mostly water, and a simple nerve net coordinates the pulsing bell while sensory structures track light and orientation. The four horseshoe shapes visible through the transparent body are reproductive organs. Tiny stinging cells on the tentacles capture plankton, although the sting is usually mild for humans. Food moves into a central digestive cavity with only one opening. Even without a central command center, the jelly can sense, feed, move, and react. It is a living reminder that a nervous system does not need a brain to organize behavior.",
