  "giant_panda": {
    "title": "A PANDA HAS A SIXTH FINGER THAT ISN'T A FINGER",
    "script": "A giant panda grips bamboo with something that looks like a thumb, but it is actually an enlarged wrist bone covered by a fleshy pad. This pseudo-thumb presses stalks against the true fingers while powerful jaws crush the fibers. The panda belongs to the order Carnivora and still has a digestive system more like a meat eater's than a specialized herbivore's. Bamboo passes through inefficiently, so the animal spends much of the day eating enormous quantities and resting to conserve energy. Its famous body plan is therefore a collection of compromises: a bear-like ancestor remodeled just enough to survive on a difficult grass.",
